  "slug": "diana-microrna-cb45",
  "summary": "Small-RNA and long-read datasets are being reorganized into queryable resources that link regulators, targets and transcript isoforms.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the construction of curated, queryable resources that make regulatory and transcript evidence interpretable. Argonomics Explorer integrates public sRNA-seq datasets to query AGO-sRNA and AGO-target interactions in C. elegans, while miRTarBase 11.0 organizes experimentally supported miRNA-target interactions around the approach that generated each record, reflecting that different experimental methods capture distinct interaction types. For transcript isoforms, IsoAtlas provides interactive visualization of long-read evidence from 1035 human and 414 mouse samples, and MIsoTEx classifies mammalian isoforms by tissue distribution, expression stability and abundance. The novelty lies in interactive, evidence-linked access to these data rather than static compilation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-28"
}
